---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import About from '../components/About.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Sponsors from '../components/Sponsors.astro';

const organizers = (await getCollection('authors'))
	.filter((entry) => entry.id.startsWith('en/'))
	.map((entry) => entry.data);
---

<PageLayout title="About Summit" description="The people and partners bringing a climate summit to Mexico City.">
	<section class="content-shell py-12 space-y-14">
		<About lang="en" />

		<section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-border pb-14 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.25fr)_minmax(16rem,0.75fr)]" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
			<div class="space-y-5">
				<p class="eyebrow m-0">The gathering</p>
				<h1 id="about-heading" class="m-0 text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">A summit for the work that happens after the climate report.</h1>
				<p class="m-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Summit is a focused gathering for people working on the climate crisis: the scientists reading changes in our atmosphere, the communities protecting their territories, the organizers building fairer systems, and the practitioners turning evidence into action.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">We bring these perspectives together because a livable future will not be built by one discipline alone. It depends on honest trade-offs, shared knowledge, and the willingness to listen to the people already experiencing the effects of a changing climate.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">Across the program, speakers share the details behind their work: what they have learned, what changed their mind, and what can be done next. The aim is not a catalogue of perfect answers. It is a more useful conversation about how to move from concern to collective action.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="space-y-5 border-l-0 border-border pt-1 lg:border-l lg:pl-8">
				<p class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">Built for attention, not alarm.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">The schedule leaves space between sessions for questions, chance conversations, and a proper break. Two rooms keep the program varied while leaving room to process difficult evidence and imagine practical responses.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">Mexico City gives the gathering a powerful setting: a living capital, the forests of Chapultepec, and a museum made for connecting human history with the future of the Earth.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-6" aria-labelledby="organizers-heading">
			<header class="max-w-2xl space-y-2">
				<p class="eyebrow m-0">Organizers</p>
				<h1 id="organizers-heading" class="m-0 text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">The people behind Summit</h1>
				<p class="m-0 text-muted">A small local team shaping a thoughtful, practical gathering for people working toward climate justice.</p>
			</header>
			<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
				{organizers.map((organizer) => <Card title={organizer.name} eyebrow={organizer.role} description={organizer.bio} image={organizer.avatar} imageAlt={organizer.name} />)}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-y border-border py-10" aria-labelledby="sponsors-heading">
			<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
				<p class="eyebrow m-0">Sponsors</p>
				<h2 id="sponsors-heading" class="m-0 text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink">Help make Summit possible</h2>
				<p class="m-0 text-muted">Sponsorship supports accessible tickets, a welcoming venue, and the practical details that make a climate gathering possible. Partner opportunities will be announced soon.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="mt-8">
				<Sponsors />
			</div>
		</section>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
